<DocPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  description="How the Theory of Economic Relativity website collects, uses, and protects information from visitors."
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 29, 2026</p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>This policy describes how the Theory of Economic Relativity ("TER") website collects and uses information from visitors. TER is an open research project, not a company selling a product or service, and this site collects very little information as a result.</p>

  <h2>Information you provide</h2>
  <p>The only place this site asks you for information is the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. It collects an email address (required), an optional name, and the message you write. Submitting the form is voluntary — nothing else on the site asks you to enter personal information.</p>

  <h2>How the contact form is processed</h2>
  <p>Contact form submissions are sent directly to <a href="https://usebasin.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">UseBasin</a>, a third-party form-processing service, which delivers the message to the site operator. UseBasin, not this website, receives and stores the submitted data on its own systems; review UseBasin's own terms and privacy practices if you want details on how they handle it.</p>

  <h2>Automatically collected information</h2>
  <p>This site is a static website. Whatever infrastructure hosts it may automatically log standard technical information common to any web request — such as IP address, browser or device information, and the pages requested — for operating and securing the service. This repository does not configure or control any such logging itself, and no specific hosting provider or retention practice is documented here.</p>

  <h2>Cookies, analytics, and tracking</h2>
  <p>This site does not use cookies, analytics, or tracking scripts of any kind. The only piece of information the site itself stores in your browser is a light/dark theme preference, saved using your browser's local storage. That preference stays on your device — it is never sent to a server, and no other data is stored this way.</p>

  <h2>How information is used</h2>
  <p>Information submitted through the contact form is used solely to read and respond to your message. It is not used for advertising, sold, or shared with anyone beyond what's needed to deliver and respond to your message (i.e., UseBasin, as described above).</p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Aside from UseBasin (contact form processing) and the site's hosting infrastructure, this site does not load third-party trackers, embedded widgets, or social plugins. The site links out to other destinations, including GitHub — see "External links" below.</p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>This site does not operate a database and does not itself retain contact form submissions once they are sent — they are handled directly by UseBasin. We don't have a fixed retention schedule to publish here; if you'd like a submission removed, contact us through the form and we'll do what we reasonably can given that it's processed by a third party.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>No method of transmission over the internet or method of electronic storage is completely secure. While reasonable care is taken in how this site is built and operated, we cannot guarantee absolute security of any information you send.</p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>This site links to external destinations, including its GitHub repository. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which this policy does not cover. Review their policies directly before sharing information with them.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>This policy may be updated from time to time as the site changes. The "Last updated" date above reflects the most recent revision; check back here for the current version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or a request regarding your information should go through the <a href="/contact/">website contact form</a> rather than a public email address.</p>
</DocPage>
